:null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"30","left":244,"top":1268.5,"alignX":244,"alignY":1284.5,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"define","target":{"k":"var","name":"I.s"},"value":{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"real","v":2.5},{"k":"op","op":"pow","args":[{"k":"real","v":10},{"k":"real","v":-9}]}]},{"k":"id","name":"A"}]},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"31","left":364,"top":1268.5,"alignX":364,"alignY":1284.5,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"define","target":{"k":"var","name":"n"},"value":{"k":"real","v":1.75},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"32","left":434,"top":1268.5,"alignX":434,"alignY":1284.5,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"define","target":{"k":"var","name":"V.T"},"value":{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"real","v":25.85},{"k":"id","name":"mV"}]},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"33","left":54,"top":1306.5,"alignX":54,"alignY":1326.5,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"define","target":{"k":"var","name":"I"},"value":{"k":"op","op":"minus","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"op","op":"div","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"n"},{"k":"id","name":"V.T"}]},{"k":"id","name":"R"}]},{"k":"call","fn":{"k":"id","name":"LambertW"},"args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"op","op":"div","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"I.s"},{"k":"id","name":"R"}]},{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"n"},{"k":"id","name":"V.T"}]}]},{"k":"op","op":"pow","args":[{"k":"id","name":"e"},{"k":"op","op":"div","args":[{"k":"op","op":"plus","args":[{"k":"id","name":"V"},{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"I.s"},{"k":"id","name":"R"}]}]},{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"n"},{"k":"id","name":"V.T"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"k":"id","name":"I.s"}]},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"34","left":384,"top":1310.5,"alignX":384,"alignY":1326.5,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"eval","expr":{"k":"id","name":"I"},"stored":null,"unit":{"k":"id","name":"mA"}}},{"id":"36","left":54,"top":1374,"alignX":54,"alignY":1394,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"define","target":{"k":"var","name":"V.d"},"value":{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"n"},{"k":"id","name":"V.T"}]},{"k":"call","fn":{"k":"id","name":"ln"},"args":[{"k":"op","op":"plus","args":[{"k":"op","op":"div","args":[{"k":"id","name":"I"},{"k":"id","name":"I.s"}]},{"k":"real","v":1}]}]}]},"global":false,"stored":null,"unit":null,"shown":false}},{"id":"37","left":274,"top":1378,"alignX":274,"alignY":1394,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"eval","expr":{"k":"id","name":"V.d"},"stored":null,"unit":null}},{"id":"38","left":394,"top":1378,"alignX":394,"alignY":1394,"disabled":false,"content":{"k":"eval","expr":{"k":"op","op":"plus","args":[{"k":"op","op":"mult","args":[{"k":"id","name":"I"},{"k":"id","name":"R"}]},{"k":"id","name":"V.d"}]},"stored":null,"unit":null}}],"texts":[{"id":"1","left":54,"top":72,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"Some integrals and equations come up so often that their answers have names. Three of them, each answering a question that has no answer in elementary functions."},{"id":"2","left":54,"top":107,"width":440,"height":67.5,"text":"Light past a straight edge. Green light, λ = 500 nm, passes the edge of a razor blade and falls on a screen 1 m beyond. Geometry says the shadow is sharp; in fact bright and dark fringes run along the lit side and light reaches into the shadow. With the distance x from the edge scaled to v, the brightness, relative to the light with no blade, is built from the Fresnel integrals:"},{"id":"11","left":54,"top":508.5,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"At the edge of the geometric shadow the brightness is a quarter; the first bright fringe, 37% brighter than no blade at all, is about 0.6 mm out:"},{"id":"14","left":54,"top":581.5,"width":440,"height":40.5,"text":"The Cornu spiral on the right is FresnelC against FresnelS, winding into (½, ½) and (−½, −½); the brightness is the square of the distance along it from (−½, −½). Each integral's derivative is the function inside it:"},{"id":"17","left":54,"top":864,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"The Gibbs overshoot. A square wave summed from its first N odd harmonics overshoots its edges, and adding harmonics only squeezes the overshoot closer to the edge without shrinking it."},{"id":"22","left":384,"top":975,"width":164,"height":60,"text":"Near the edge at 0, the sum peaks at the first zero of its derivative, x = π/(2N), and the height there tends to (2/π)·Si(π) as N grows."},{"id":"26","left":54,"top":1167,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"The wave jumps from −1 to 1, so it overshoots by 0.179, about 9% of the jump, however many harmonics are added."},{"id":"27","left":54,"top":1220,"width":440,"height":40.5,"text":"A diode and a resistor. A small silicon diode in series with 100 Ω across 5 V: its current I obeys V = I·R + n·V_T·ln(I/I_s + 1), which has no answer in elementary functions. Lambert's W, the w for which w·eʷ = a, gives it exactly."},{"id":"35","left":54,"top":1352.5,"width":440,"height":13.5,"text":"A check: the diode's voltage, and the two voltages adding up to 5 V again."},{"id":"39","left":54,"top":1420,"width":440,"height":27,"text":"MathMath gives all of these with =. In Mathcad 14 the Fresnel integrals, Si and LambertW are symbolic-only, so there the numbers come from → with the float keyword."}],"opaque":[],"origin":0,"tol":0.001,"exactCompare":true,"zeroOverZero":false,"otherRegions":{},"componentOutputs":[]}}